[Round 1/8 | Implementer | 552.4s | 0/400k] I’m replacing the lock with a fixed pool of exactly `capacity` atomic occupancy tokens. A token’s single atomic word carries FREE/RESERVED/PUBLISHED plus the owning lane/slot, so a paused producer has already made a globally visible reservation that any later consumer can publish-help. A bitmap and consumer-local heap keep normal dequeue work bounded by published items rather than scanning every lane on every call.

